                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers [/h1]\n\nThis game sucks. You don't have to take my word for it, just look at the store page video starting at 1:10. That's basically the game. Yeah, shooting stuff looks that awful. This is a full locomotion game with puzzles and climbing and zero-gravity and some bland story.\n\nBut at its core it's still a wave shooter. A pretty awful one. Enemies spawn out of nowhere, everywhere. You spam a slow motion ability over and over again. You switch weapons and they automatically reload, next time you get to it. Neat! Constant carnage. And enemies just keep coming, over and over and over again. Infnite & quick spawns in some areas. \n\nThe puzzles are very simple and crude and look awful. I actually did get stuck, not because the puzzle was difficult, but because the game gave no indication of how to proceed. Then I looked at the store page video and saw the solution. You're supposed to move floating barrels to these washing machine looking contraptions to unlock the door. I would never have figured that out because the graphics are so bad that I never would have guessed those floating barrels even fit there and much less they were they key to unlocking the hatch. \n\nThe climbing also feels not so great, but at least it's not glitchy. Zero-gravity was okay I guess. The enemies look bad. In fact all the graphics look bad. Enemies are bullet sponges. You have to almost unload your whole clip into some of them. You just run away, shoot, change weapon, slow motion, shoot some more. Rinse and repeat. Over and over and over again. All enemies just walk/run towards you.\n\nThe mission mode is just the old version of the game, a boring wave shooter, except you can move within a limited area. The graphics look much better in mission mode. The environments are top notch. But the combat is just as bad as campaign mode, plus there's less variety. \n\nRate 4.5/10. They devs tried so that's good, but just overall sloppy execution. This is a $1.99 budget game at best in its current state. This is B movie quality. Recommended only for for Twitch streamers or YouTubers for Let's Play and make loud noises and make fun of the game type deal.",
